worktrees/agent-a11c0a040e3cf682b","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"claude/capabilities-matrix-impl-2a0cfd"}
{"parentUuid":"b864b8fc-846f-4fae-8d1f-c62382bf72fa","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6b8557a2-9430-4f17-946a-1ea07dab5643","agentId":"a11c0a040e3cf682b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012tbUFqm3gxNdCQAt1sLW4J","type":"tool_result","content":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# The ONLY writer of cursor-mock/snapshots/ (the snapshots-read-only gate\n# refuses every other write). Everything it writes is sealed; snapshots-current\n# refuses a snapshot whose seal does not match, so a hand edit is caught at the\n# commit even if it slipped past the gate.\n#\n#   capture.sh run <name>    run the scenario in runs/<name>/setup/ against the\n#                            real `cursor-agent`, and add a sample\n#   capture.sh doc <url>     freeze a doc page (e.g. https://cursor.com/docs/hooks):\n#                            its sha256 goes in the MANIFEST; its text only into a cache\n#                            under the git dir, never into the repo\n#   capture.sh drop <run> <ts>  remove one sample (a bad or non-hermetic capture)\n#   capture.sh all           re-capture every run and doc at the installed\n#                            cursor-agent's version, and set MANIFEST.version to it\n#\n# The version is cursor-agent's release date (`2026.09.28`): `--version` also\n# prints a build hash after it (`2026.09.28-64d2043`), which the schema's\n# version pattern does not take, so the hash is dropped.\n#\n# Login: cursor-agent has no environment-only login in this setup, so the fake\n# HOME links to the user's Keychains directory and nothing else (the same as\n# claude-mock's capture). No credential is copied into the fake HOME; the\n# email the login reports is nulled out of every payload before anything is\n# sealed. A CURSOR_API_KEY is never read or passed.\n#\n# A scenario is hand-authored, and only its setup/ is:\n#   runs/<name>/setup/prompt.txt       the prompt\n#   runs/<name>/setup/hooks.json       the project's .cursor/hooks.json\n#   runs/<name>/setup/*.sh             optional: the hook scripts, installed in .cursor/hooks/;\n#                                      hook.sh appends to $HOOK_LOG\n#   runs/<name>/setup/args             optional: extra cursor-agent flags, one per line\n#   runs/<name>/setup/env              optional: KEY=VALUE lines cursor-agent inherits on\n#                                      top of the hermetic env\nset -euo pipefail\nhere=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\nmanifest=\"$here/MANIFEST.yaml\"\ndie() { echo \"capture.sh: $*\" >&2; exit 1; }\nversion() { yq -r '.version' \"$manifest\"; }\ninstalled() { cursor-agent --version | awk '{print $1}' | sed 's/-.*$//'; }\n# The first capture creates the MANIFEST, frozen at the installed version: it is\n{\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"sessionStart\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"sessionEnd\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"preToolUse\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"postToolUse\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"postToolUseFailure\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"subagentStart\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"subagentStop\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"beforeShellExecution\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"afterShellExecution\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"beforeMCPExecution\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"afterMCPExecution\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"beforeReadFile\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"afterFileEdit\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"beforeSubmitPrompt\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"preCompact\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"stop\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"afterAgentResponse\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }],\n    \"afterAgentThought\": [{ \"command\": \".cursor/hooks/hook.sh\" }]\n  }\n}\n#!/bin/sh\n# Every event logs its payload.\nIN=$(cat)\nprintf '%s\\n' \"$IN\" >>\"$HOOK_LOG\"\nexit 0\nDo these as separate tool calls, one per call, in order: 1) create the file note.txt containing the word hi, with your file edit/write tool, not the shell 2) read the file note.txt with your Read tool 3) change the word hi in note.txt to bye, with your file edit tool, not the shell. Then reply only DONE.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c52fe137-2727-4591-b312-f9ec086160f1","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:46:03.807Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b864b8fc-846f-4fae-8d1f-c62382bf72fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a11c0a040e3cf682b","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"claude/capabilities-matrix-impl-2a0cfd"}
