checks 2.435s, judges 0s\nsloprail: file-guard \"module-boundaries\": cheap checks 6.075s, judges 0s\nsloprail: file-guard \"module-coverage\": cheap checks 18.694s, judges 0s\nsloprail: file-guard \"module-distinct\": cheap checks 52ms, judges 53.104s\nsloprail: file-guard \"module-leaks\": cheap checks 52ms, judges 41.348s\nsloprail: file-guard \"module-leaks\": cheap checks 50ms, judges 48.353s\nsloprail: file-guard \"module-leaks\": cheap checks 51ms, judges 28.585s\nsloprail: file-guard \"shapes\": cheap checks 1.189s, judges 0s\nsloprail: file-guard \"snapshots-current\": cheap checks 15.012s, judges 0s\nsloprail: file-guard \"snapshots-current\": cheap checks 5.436s, judges 0s\nsloprail: file-guard \"snapshots-current\": cheap checks 5.866s, judges 0s\nsloprail: file-guards evaluated in 38m28.317s (26 rules, concurrency 6)\nthe following rules refused this work:\n  - Codex is listed as supported with no deviations, but its PostToolUse doc table (tool_name, tool_use_id, tool_input, tool_response) has no duration field and its recorded payloads (codex-mock/snapshots/runs/stops, posttool-block) carry no duration, with tool_response a plain string like \"FINE\n  - The claim that whatever the hook prints is not recorded in the transcript is grounded for neither codex nor cursor: the cited runs use hook scripts that print nothing on sessionEnd (codex hook.sh only appends to HOOK_LOG; cursor hook.sh prints nothing for sessionEnd), and the docs only say output is advisory or \"logged but not used\" (codex: \"their output won't steer Codex\"; cursor: \"The response is logged but not used\"), which says nothing about the transcript.\n  - Codex is cited as supported, but the statement's part 'the background tasks still running' is neither stated in its Stop doc (fields are only turn_id, stop_hook_active, last_assistant_message) nor shown in codex-mock/snapshots/runs/stops (Stop payloads have no background-tasks field), and the codex cell lists no deviation for it.\n  - Codex is cited as supported with no deviations, but its doc section (developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#userpromptsubmit) and its two runs (hook-exit-codes, prompt-blocked) never state or show two parts of the statement: that the hook cannot rewrite the prompt (the doc only says plain stdout or additionalContext is added as developer context, and decision block / exit 2 blocks it), and that it also fires for a background-task notification handed to the agent (no doc line, and neither run has a background task or a UserPromptSubmit payload for a notification). Either ground those parts with a doc or run, list them as codex deviations, or drop them from the statement.\n  - codex: the docs state that SessionStart hooks matching source \"compact\" add additionalContext to the continuation after compaction, and that background (async: true) hooks' additionalContext is added to the model's context at the next safe point. No test covers either, the codex mock has no compaction or async handling, and the codex subject declares no deviation for them.\n  - hook-command-handler/codex: the doc (hooks#config-shape) says commands run with the session cwd and that Codex may be started from a subdirectory, but TestCommandHookReadsThePayloadOnStdinInTheSessionDirectory only ever starts the mock at the repo root, so it would still pass if the mock ran hooks from the git root or project root instead of the session cwd; no test starts the mock from a subdirectory and checks that hooks run there and the payload cwd matches.\n  - cursor: the recorded tool-failure payloads carry a cwd field (cwd is the empty string on preToolUse and beforeShellExecution, and the docs list cwd on preToolUse), but TestEveryHookPayloadNamesTheSessionTheTranscriptAndTheWorkspace asserts only session_id, conversation_id, workspace_roots and transcript_path, so no test checks the cwd the mock puts in tool and shell payloads. The codex subject checks out.\n  - noninteractive-run/codex: the doc says 'Codex streams progress to stderr and prints only the final agent message to stdout', but TestExecWithoutJSONPrintsOnlyTheFinalMessage asserts only stdout. No test checks the stderr side, and the mock writes only tool-error lines to stderr, with no progress. No deviation declares that gap, so it needs a test and a run, or a deviation.\n  - posttooluse-payload/codex is only tested for one successful Bash call; the doc says PostToolUse also fires for Bash commands that exit non-zero (and for apply_patch, MCP and other tools) and no test checks that, and the test does not assert the recorded payload fields hook_event_name, session_id or permission_mode. posttooluse-payload/cursor replays only file-tools, so the recorded Shell postToolUse payload (tool_input.timeout, tool_output exitCode JSON) is not asserted. No cursor test asserts that a failed or denied call fires postToolUseFailure instead of postToolUse.\n  - session-start-hook/codex: the only proving test (TestSessionStartSaysStartupAndCannotStopTheSession) never checks that the SessionStart matcher is applied to source, although runs/hook-matchers records the matcher \"startup\" hook running (\"ran\":\"session-startup\") while the \"resume\" one does not, and the docs say \"matcher is applied to source\"; it also asserts nothing else of the recorded payload (session_id, hook_event_name, permission_mode) or that a startup-matching hook fires first.\n  - TestStopBlockContinuesTheTurnWithOneEnd (codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/capabilities_test.go) only checks that the rollout merely contains BLOCK-JSON-REASON and BLOCK-EXIT2-REASON, which would also pass if the reason were logged somewhere other than handed to the agent; it never asserts the reason arrives as a new user-role prompt (doc: 'acts as a new user prompt'), that the agent actually produced further agent_message items after each block (runs/stops stream shows several agent_messages before the single turn.completed), or the stop_hook_active false->true->true sequence on the continuations; it also has no test for the plain exit-2 stderr block (runs/hook-exit-codes) as a standalone case, and it does not assert the final turn.completed comes after the last Stop hook.\n  - TestStopPayloadCarriesLastMessageAndContinuing asserts last_assistant_message only on the first Stop (DONE) and never on the continued Stop (recorded \"DONE2\" with stop_hook_active=true), and no test checks the Stop payload field turn_id that the doc (hooks#stop) lists and every recorded Stop payload carries.\n  - subprocess-session-env/codex: the recorded tool command and hook both saw CODEX_MANAGED_BY_NPM=1 and CODEX_MANAGED_PACKAGE_ROOT (how the harness was started), and in nested-session-env CODEX_MANAGED_BY_NPM=1 overrode the decoy value (PostToolUse tool_response in events.jsonl), but the codex mock never sets these variables (no match in codex-mock Go sources) and no test checks them; sessionVars in env_test.go compares only CODEX_CI, CODEX_SESSION_ID, CODEX_THREAD_ID and CODEX_VERSION, and the hook test checks only CODEX_HOME. The recorded CODEX_SANDBOX=decoy passthrough is also unchecked.\n\n[exited with code 0]","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"fed5211f-f026-4721-b4be-280393ff9640","timestamp":"2026-10-03T15:44:13.063Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"02916025-40f7-4a95-9d06-1db60297c0fc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a11c0a040e3cf682b","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a7e54ea3099505a7e"}
