{"parentUuid":"522f043a-3170-42a5-845d-22e2f9d0fe01","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a11c0a040e3cf682b","attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a11c0a040e3cf682b/codex-mock/internal/runner/tool_host.go","snippet":"53\t\n54\t// Execute runs the command and shows it in the event stream.\n55\tfunc (h toolHost) Execute(ctx context.Context, c toolcall.Call) toolcall.Result {\n56\t\tif c.Name == spawnTool {\n57\t\t\treturn h.spawnExecute(c)\n58\t\t}\n59\t\tcmd := command(c)\n60\t\tid := h.events.CommandStarted(cmd)\n61\t\tvar r tools.BashResult\n62\t\tif y := yieldTime(c); y > 0 {\n63\t\t\tvar running bool\n64\t\t\tif r, running = h.runYielding(cmd, y); running {\n65\t\t\t\treturn toolcall.Result{Output: r.Output} // still running: no end to report\n66\t\t\t}\n67\t\t} else {\n68\t\t\tr = tools.Bash(ctx, cmd, h.cfg.Cwd, h.toolEnv)\n69\t\t}\n70\t\th.events.CommandCompleted(id, cmd, r.Output, r.ExitCode)\n71\t\treturn toolcall.Result{Output: r.Output, Failed: r.Failed()}\n72\t}\n73\t\n74\t// After fires PostToolUse, which Codex fires for every command that ran,\n75\t// whatever its exit status; a hook that blocks (exit 2, or a block decision)\n76\t// gives the agent its feedback in place of the result.\n77\t// sr:provides posttooluse-payload/codex"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5fa48e73-665a-41a9-9751-3f569bb07ea5","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:24:05.389Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a11c0a040e3cf682b/codex-mock/internal/runner/tool_host.go changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n53\t\n54\t// Execute runs the command and shows it in the event stream.\n55\tfunc (h toolHost)