{"parentUuid":"2f9f8f27-c9d2-44ad-8f5a-cda377af47b0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a11c0a040e3cf682b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014gTfbkTf2QyrEXq9Mef6Xv","type":"tool_result","content":"25:| During a turn                     | `PreToolUse`, `PermissionRequest`, `PostToolUse`, `PreCompact`, `PostCompact`, `UserPromptSubmit`, `SubagentStop`, `Stop` |\n26:| When you interrupt an active turn | `Interrupt` (doesn't run for subagents)                                                                                   |\n27:| When a session or subagent starts | `SessionStart`, `SubagentStart`                                                                                           |\n28:| When the main thread ends         | `SessionEnd` (doesn't run for subagents)                                                                                  |\n85:  `SubagentStart`, or `Stop`\n427:| `SubagentStart`     | subagent type          | Values depend on the subagent that starts                    |\n428:| `SubagentStop`      | subagent type          | Values depend on the subagent that stops                     |\n475:| `session_id`      | `string`         | Current Codex session id. Subagent hooks use the parent session id. |\n485:`UserPromptSubmit`, `SubagentStart`, `SubagentStop`, `Stop`, and `Interrupt` also include\n497:`SubagentStop`, and `Stop` support these shared JSON fields. `SubagentStart`\n1:# Hooks\n30:## Where Codex looks for hooks\n62:## Review and trust hooks\n80:## Config shape\n230:## MCP tool hooks\n236:### Configure an MCP tool hook\n272:### Expand arguments from the hook event\n299:### Execution and lifecycle\n312:## Turn hooks off\n325:## Managed hooks from `requirements.toml`\n375:## Plugin-bundled hooks\n410:## Matcher patterns\n445:### Tool coverage\n467:## Common input fields\n494:## Common output fields\n527:### Large hook output\n568:## Run hooks in the backg