{"parentUuid":"c025fff0-f1d1-49de-b51c-857fafcbbffc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a11c0a040e3cf682b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014RQq8JmQgQEWNyjg4RrKuc","type":"tool_result","content":"13:- Control subagent (Task tool) execution\n28:- `subagentStart` / `subagentStop` - Subagent (Task tool) lifecycle\n69:| `subagentStart`        | Yes       |\n70:| `subagentStop`         | Yes       |\n194:- Exit code `0` - Hook succeeded, use the JSON output. For permission hooks (`beforeShellExecution`, `beforeMCPExecution`, `beforeReadFile`, `beforeTabFileRead`, `subagentStart`, `preToolUse`), invalid JSON or a response that doesn't match the hook's schema blocks the action.\n676:    \"subagentStart\": [{ \"command\": \"./hooks/validate-subagent.sh\" }],\n677:    \"subagentStop\": [{ \"command\": \"./hooks/audit-subagent.sh\" }],\n691:The Agent hooks (`sessionStart`, `sessionEnd`, `preToolUse`, `postToolUse`, `postToolUseFailure`, `subagentStart`, `subagentStop`, `beforeShellExecution`, `afterShellExecution`, `beforeMCPExecution`, `afterMCPExecution`, `beforeReadFile`, `afterFileEdit`, `beforeSubmitPrompt`, `preCompact`, `stop`, `afterAgentResponse`, `afterAgentThought`) apply to Cmd+K and Agent Chat operations. The Tab hooks (`beforeTabFileRead`, `afterTabFileEdit`) apply specifically to inline Tab completions. The app lifecycle hook (`workspaceOpen`) fires when a workspace opens and on workspace folder changes, independent of any agent session.\n706:| `loop_limit` | number \\| null            | `5`              | Per-script loop limit for stop/subagentStop hooks. `null` means no limit. Default is `5` for Cursor hooks, `null` for Claude Code hooks.                                                                                                                 |\n724:    \"subagentStart\": [\n740:- **subagentStart**: The matcher runs against the **subagent type** (e.g. `explore`, `shell`, `generalPurpose`). Use it to run hooks only when a specific kind of subagent is started. The example above runs `validate-explore.sh` only for explore or shell subagents.\n746:- **subagentStart / subagentStop**: Filter by subagent type (`generalPurpose`, `explore`, `shell`, etc.).\n956:#### subagentStart\n958:Called before spawning a subagent (Task tool). Can allow or deny subagent creation.\n963:  \"subagent_id\": \"abc-123\",\n964:  \"subagent_type\": \"generalPurpose\",\n968:  \"subagent_model\": \"claude-sonnet-4-20250514\",\n982:| `subagent_id`            | string            | Unique identifier for this subagent instance                 |\n983:| `subagent_type`          | string            | Type of subagent: `generalPurpose`, `explore`, `shell`, etc. |\n984:| `task`                   | string            | The task description given to the subagent                   |\n986:| `tool_call_id`           | string            | ID of the tool call that triggered the subagent              |\n987:| `subagent_model`         | string            | Model the subagent will use                                  |\n988:| `is_parallel_worker`     | boolean           | Whether this subagent is running as a parallel worker        |\n989:| `git_branch`             | string (optional) | Git branch the subagent will operate on, if applicable       |\n993:| `permission`   | string            | `\"allow\"` to proceed, `\"deny\"` to block. `\"ask\"` is not supported for `subagentStart` and is treated as `\"deny\"`. |\n994:| `user_message` | string (optional) | Message shown to the user when the subagent is denied                                                             |\n996:#### subagentStop\n998:Called when a subagent completes, errors, or is aborted. Can trigger follow-up actions.\n1003:  \"subagent_type\": \"generalPurpose\",\n1007:  \"summary\": \"<subagent output summary>\",\n\n`SessionStart`, `PreToolUse`, `PermissionRequest`, `PostToolUse`,\n`UserPromptSubmit`, `SubagentStart`, `SubagentStop`, `Stop`, and `Interrupt` also include\n`permission_mode`, which describes the current permission mode as `default`,\n`acceptEdits`, `plan`, `dontAsk`, or `bypassPermissions`.\n\n`transcript_path` points to a chat transcript for convenience, but the\ntranscript format isn't a stable interface for hooks and may change over time.\n\nIf you need the full wire format, see [Schemas](#schemas).","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"da3690d4-55c7-4332-921d-f27134f440e9","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:35:29.961Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c025fff0-f1d1-49de-b51c-857fafcbbffc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a11c0a040e3cf682b","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-adc1470310079e23b"}
