pshots/runs/background-agent/samples/20261003-145116/events.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/background-agent/samples/20261003-145116/exit.txt, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/background-agent/samples/20261003-145116/payloads.jsonl (and 23 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n219:  - Where does a run's background-task registry live, and who shuts it down? codex-mock/internal/runner/spawn_agent.go (`var agents = tasks.NewRegistry()` plus `func EndAgents() { agents.Shutdown() }`, called from `defer runner.EndAgents()` in codex-mock/exec.go) and cursor-mock/internal/runner/subagent_run.go (`var agents = tasks.NewRegistry()`) make it a package-level global that lives as long as the process. The same codex runner already keeps a per-run registry (`bg: tasks.NewRegistry()` with `defer s.bg.Shutdown()` in run.go), and claude-mock does the same (`backgroundTasks{Registry: tasks.NewRegistry()}`), so the codebase now handles this two different ways. Checklist: global registry: undecided; spawn/Task tools, collab events and agent_id/agent_type in the payload: local, following recorded runs; sub-agent run via turnloop/toolcall/tasks: covered by the turnloop, toolcall and tasks modules; time.Now() for the rollout: follows existing use. No ADR decides this. Ask the user to decide it (a new ADR), or which existing ADR it falls under. (file-guard \"concern-undeclared\")\n220-exit 1","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"06155079-4238-4e3c-902b-334adab8e18c","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:35:42.563Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a420cc6f-e62c-4969-bf94-8c897a77f751","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a11c0a040e3cf682b","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-adc1470310079e23b"}
