{"parentUuid":"fe83da2b-a2eb-43c6-b70e-43c509152a70","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a11c0a040e3cf682b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V2HnC5Jdg8Kb9wDF7R7hxZ","type":"tool_result","content":"  codex:\n    docs:\n      - https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#common-input-fields\n    runs:\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/background-agent\n    deviations:\n      - adr: capability-grounding\n        statement: >-\n          Codex's spawn_agent has no foreground or background choice: it\n          always answers at once with a receipt (the sub-agent's id and a\n          nickname) and the sub-agent runs concurrently with the turn, its\n          hooks firing under the same session id with an agent_id and an\n          agent_type (recorded: runs/background-agent).\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The mock's spawn_agent is told by a parameter of its own, background,\n          that the dispatch is not waited for (without it the mock waits for\n          the sub-agent and answers as a following wait would); the sub-agent\n          runs on its own thread and rollout, driven by the scenario script it\n          is given, and is stopped if still running when the run ends. The\n          sub-agent's states after pending_init, a sub-agent's own dispatches\n          of sub-agents, and what the agent is told when a hook refuses the\n          spawn, are not modelled.\n  cursor:\n    docs:\n      - https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#subagentstart","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f877c1ca-95ae-4676-a45d-cc029515d455","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:51:20.088Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fe83da2b-a2eb-43c6-b70e-43c509152a70","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a11c0a040e3cf682b","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a5