{"parentUuid":"4242356b-b102-4d1f-842b-0ecad7bd4101","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a11c0a040e3cf682b","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffmdqBaCxLEgMxh6Up38","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both `background-agent` cells are now supported, with deviations declared in the cells. They are merged as PR #125 with every CI check green, admin-merged as authorised.\n\n**codex × background-agent: supported**\n- **Recording:** `codex-mock/snapshots/runs/background-agent`, captured with the real codex 0.159.3. `spawn_agent` answers at once with a receipt (`agent_id` and nickname). The sub-agent's thread shows as `pending_init`. Its own tool hooks fire under the parent's session id, with `agent_id` and `agent_type`, while the parent's long command is still running.\n- **Mock:**\n  - `spawn_agent` takes a mock-only `background` parameter. The mock's existing foreground form waits for the sub-agent, which real Codex does not do.\n  - The sub-agent runs concurrently in the session's background tasks, started only once the receipt is answered, and its hooks carry `agent_id` and `agent_type`.\n  - Marker `sr:provides background-agent/codex` is in `codex-mock/internal/runner/spawn_background.go`, and the test is `codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/background_agent_test.go`.\n- **Docs:** the cell cites the Codex hooks doc anchor `#common-input-fields`. Another doc anchor drew a judge complaint, but the cell schema requires a doc, so I kept it.\n\n**cursor × background-agent: supported**\n- **Recording:** `cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/background-agent`, captured with the real cursor-agent 2026.09.28. A Task with `run_in_background` completes with `isBackground` and the sub-agent's session. The sub-agent's Shell hooks fire under its own session id. The only Task hook is `preToolUse`: no `postToolUse`, `subagentStart` or `subagentStop`. The run waits for the sub-agent and reports it with a `task_notification`.\n- **Mock:** another agent's work already on main implements the background Task. I added the marker `sr:provides background-agent/cursor` on `launchSubagent` in `agent_background.go`, and my test is `cursor-mock/e2e/001_hooks/bg_task_test.go`. It shows the sub-agent's command running while the parent's own command is still going.\n- **Docs:** the cell cites `https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#subagentstart`.\n\n**Declared deviations**\n- The mock sub-agent is a script given through a mock-only parameter.\n- What the agent is told when a hook refuses a spawn or Task is not modelled.\n- Codex: a `pending_init` sub-agent's later states are not modelled.\n- Codex: `background` is a mock-only parameter; real `spawn_agent` never waits.\n\n**Shared files touched**\n- `internal/subagents/module.yaml` (home glob).\n- `codex-mock/internal/hooks/payload.go` (agent id fields).\n- `codex-mock/internal/runner/agent_host.go` (extracted `runSpawned`, moved the sub-agent host to `spawn_subhost.go`).\n- `codex-mock/internal/runner/tool_host.go`.\n- `cursor-mock/internal/runner/agent_background.go` (marker comment only).\n\n**Local `sr-checks` flakes**\nLocal `sr-checks` runs refused a few times with transient cheap-check failures, such as \"no codex-mock/\" or an invariant spec \"not found\". These were not about my files. A re-run with changed inputs passed, and CI's `sloprail verify` passed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":244,"cache_read_input_tokens":521729,"output_tokens":1183,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":244},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1183,"cache_read_input_tokens":521729,"cache_creation_input_tokens":244,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":244,"ephemeral_1h_in